    "question": {
      ":question/id": "17b83244-2bf3-5308-95cf-8596fc3c5511",
      ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of \n$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}}}+{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}}}+{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x\\\\ &= \\int {x}^{-4/3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int {x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-4/3+1}}{(-\\frac{4}{3}+1)}+\\frac{{x}^{3+1}}{(3+1)}-\\frac{{x}^{-2+1}}{(-2+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-1/3}}{\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{-1}}{(-1)}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{1}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
