      ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of\n$-6\\sqrt[3]{x}-\\frac{6}{x^{2}}+6x.$ For real $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int\\left(-6\\sqrt[3]{x}-\\frac{6}{x^{2}}+6x\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-6x^{\\frac{1}{3}}-6x^{-2}+6x\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= -6\\int x^{\\frac{1}{3}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x-6\\int x^{-2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+6\\int x\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= -6\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{1}{3}+1}}{(\\frac{1}{3}+1)}\\right)-6\\left(\\frac{x^{-2+1}}{(-2+1)}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad +6\\left(\\frac{x^{1+1}}{(1+1)}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -\\frac{9\\sqrt[3]{x^{4}}}{2}+\\frac{6}{x}+3x^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
