      ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of\n$-2x^{2}-\\frac{3}{x^{5}}+\\frac{6}{\\sqrt[7]{x^{8}}}.$ For real $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int\\left(-2x^{2}-\\frac{3}{x^{5}}+\\frac{6}{\\sqrt[7]{x^{8}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-2x^{2}-3x^{-5}+6x^{\\frac{-8}{7}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= -2\\int x^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x-3\\int x^{-5}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+6\\int x^{\\frac{-8}{7}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= -2\\left(\\frac{x^{2+1}}{(2+1)}\\right)-3\\left(\\frac{x^{-5+1}}{(-5+1)}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad +6\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{-8}{7}+1}}{(\\frac{-8}{7}+1)}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -\\frac{2x^{3}}{3}+\\frac{3}{4x^{4}}-\\frac{42}{\\sqrt[7]{x}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
